# App Versioning

## Format
`pubspec.yaml` is the single source of truth: `version: x.y.z+b`.

- `x` MAJOR: redesigns, breaking data migrations, architectural overhauls.
- `y` MINOR: new user-facing features.
- `z` PATCH: bug fixes, hotfixes, small performance tweaks.
- `b` BUILD: integer, +1 for every build uploaded to TestFlight, Play internal track, or production. Never reuse or decrease — App Store Connect and Play Console reject duplicates.

`x.y.z` must stay numeric only. Do NOT use pre-release suffixes (`-beta.1`, `-rc.1`): iOS `CFBundleShortVersionString` rejects them. Ship betas as new build numbers via TestFlight / Play testing tracks.

## Platform files
Never hardcode versions; they must come from `pubspec.yaml`:
- Android (`android/app/build.gradle.kts`): `versionCode = flutter.versionCode`, `versionName = flutter.versionName`.
- iOS (`ios/Runner/Info.plist`): `CFBundleShortVersionString` = `$(FLUTTER_BUILD_NAME)`, `CFBundleVersion` = `$(FLUTTER_BUILD_NUMBER)`.

## Bumping (only when explicitly asked)
1. Read the current `version:` in `pubspec.yaml`.
2. Apply the requested bump; always increment `b`:
   - Patch `1.2.3+45` → `1.2.4+46`
   - Minor `1.2.3+45` → `1.3.0+46`
   - Major `1.2.3+45` → `2.0.0+46`
   - Build-only (QA/TestFlight retry) `1.2.3+45` → `1.2.3+46`
3. Update `CHANGELOG.md` (create it if missing) using [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/), newest entry on top, omitting empty sections:

```markdown
## [x.y.z+b] - YYYY-MM-DD
### Added
### Changed
### Fixed
### Removed
```

4. Leave changes uncommitted; never create git tags (see `11-no-git-commits`).

Don't bump versions during regular feature or refactor work. Don't confuse dependency constraints in `pubspec.yaml` with the app version.
